      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Lung Position in Chest



    The lungs are cone-shaped organs located
    in the thoracic cavity, with the right lung being larger and divided into three
    lobes, while the left lung is smaller due to the heart''s position. The lungs
    are suspended from the mediastinum by the lung root, which includes the bronchus,
    pulmonary artery, and veins. The apex of the right lung extends above the clavicles,
    while the left lung has a cardiac notch to accommodate the heart. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
